00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:56.100
- My first thought was like "I'll get an abortion, 
I-I'll go to Planned Parenthood

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.380
In the end, it just... when it came down to it,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.900
I realized that I couldn't do that.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.720
I understand how other people need to make that choice,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:03.840
but...umm.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.440
Yeah, I did totally consider it.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:10.280
- I really had to think about the other women in my life that have had children.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.860
For me, the first thought that came to my mind was my mom.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.740
'Cause she tried so hard to have a baby and if I were to...

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.300
have an abortion after that, it's almost like

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.200
disrespecting all the work she put in.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.400
And I was like, "Okay, I'm gonna have this baby."

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:29.140
And, then, really it came down to 'Am I going to [go for] adoption or am I gonna be a mom?'

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.400
- I planned this pregnancy. 
A lot of people might think otherwise, and

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.300
just be like  "she's just saying that because she doesn't want people to think the baby was an accident."

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.080
I can't choose for other people, you guys have your own choice,

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.760
but there are so many ways you can prevent a pregnancy.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.920
You could have done it beforehand instead of once the baby's already in there

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.960
and trying to kill off a heartbeat, because the baby has a heartbeat on his fourth week

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.780
And that's usually when everybody finds out they're pregnant.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.920
I don't have a choice for other people, so

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.700
I mean, everybody has their own choice, but personally, I'm against it

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.740
"I was educated on birth control methods before getting pregnant."

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.280
3, 2, 1...

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:10.380
Go!

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:20.140
- The way it happened with me, I mean, I grew up in like a really like Christian household

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.360
so like it was always taught like abstinence and, like,

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:27.090
my parents didn't even know that I was having sex and I mean I was using like condoms

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:31.860
but obviously, I was naive,  that that was gonna like work in the long run, which it doesn't

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:34.080
I mean, I knew that there were options out there

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.360
but it was something that was never like explained to me that I could get this so that I won't get pregnant.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:43.840
- I'm from Texas and in Texas its abstinence, abstinence, abstinence.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.380
They told us in the health class just not to have sex, so,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.100
I honestly didn't know pregnancy was so common.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:55.820
I thought like it just happened sometimes when you had sex. Sometimes you would get pregnant.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:01.840
I really do think that, that should be very mandatory in school starting in like middle school.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.040
- Yeah, I totally agree. I live in the mountains and it's really conservative up there.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.380
The schools are really small.

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:11.160
I look at like my boyfriend's little sister, she's gonna be 12

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.860
And, some of the girls in her grade are having sex and she's-she's in sixth grade.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:21.000
The information they're giving you in schools needs to adapt

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:26.340
to where we are now in society to where it's in the right grades, it's the appropriate information

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.280
they're talking about things like the implant that are somewhat new and

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:34.140
they really need to just kind of adapt it to where we are now.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:38.780
- Yeah, as teen moms we need to take our kids and teach them everything they need to know from a young age

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.590
Like I thought my mom was gonna be mad at me

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:45.200
So we need to be open so they don't like they're not like scared to come to talk to us about something, that's so normal

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:49.100
"Relationships change after you have a child."

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:50.340
3,

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:51.180
2,

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:51.980
1...

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:53.180
Go!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:04.160
- I used to be like super outgoing in like high school, in my classes and stuff. Being pregnant,

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:09.320
as like a college student like there's many times that I feel more timid to speak because I feel like people judge me more

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.620
And I mean, maybe that's something I just have to work on but like

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.620
definitely like my relationship with myself has changed a lot

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:20.920
I bet you can all relate like you meet your baby for the first time and it's like life just shifts.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:25.520
Like almost the glasses of like naiveness and childhood just kind of come off

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.440
and you see the world from like that point of view like 'you just created a life'

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:34.160
I cried immediately for my mom and how badly I treated her as a teenager before I had my daughter

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.940
And I cried for my sister, how I treated them, teachers...

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:41.800
All of the things that we were given and I was entitled to.  Now after having a kid it all changed

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.060
-- That just changed my mind! [everyone laughs]

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.360
Changed! [laughs]

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:52.300
The hardest person to tell for me when I got pregnant was my brother. We're twins.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.360
Right now he's getting ready to go to prom

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:58.620
He's a senior in high school and he's doing all this stuff that I'm missing out on.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.320
I wouldn't take it back for anything

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.580
But telling him was the hardest because we've always been so close. We've always been the same age

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:08.360
We've always had the same friends. Now that my daughter's here and she's four months old,

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.529
you know, he comes home from work

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:13.519
And he's like, "Oh hey" and he asked me to like hold her and stuff and it's really great and I love it.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.590
So relationships do change for the better also.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:24.140
Yeah, I would say for sure like, my relationship with my mom has changed like drastically before I even got pregnant like we were close

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:28.129
but like not in the sense that we shared like something like motherhood with each other

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.549
because I think that just changes everything that we now see what our

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:35.000
parents went through and what our moms went through and how they felt. My relationship

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.359
I feel with my mom has like been really good because of my pregnancy.

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:44.420
I mean originally like, of course, she's disappointed in me, but like but then she's just like excited now to become a grandma and stuff.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.460
"My baby's father is still involved in our lives."

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:50.460
3,

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:51.400
2,

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:52.380
1...

